---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Configuration" description="All lean-ctx config.toml options explained.">
  <h1>Configuration</h1>
  <p>lean-ctx is configured via <code>~/.config/lean-ctx/config.toml</code>. Most settings have sensible defaults — you typically don't need to change anything.</p>

  <h2>File Location</h2>
  <pre><code># Default location:
~/.config/lean-ctx/config.toml

# Open in editor:
lean-ctx config edit

# Show current config:
lean-ctx config show</code></pre>

  <h2>Compression</h2>
  <pre><code>[compression]
# Global compression level: off | lite | standard | max
level = "standard"  # default

# AST languages (tree-sitter)
# Supported: rust, python, javascript, typescript, go, java, c, cpp,
#            ruby, php, swift, kotlin, scala, haskell, lua, zig, elixir, bash
languages = "all"</code></pre>

  <h2>Integration</h2>
  <pre><code>[integration]
# Mode: auto | cli-redirect | hybrid | mcp
mode = "auto"  # auto-selects based on detected tool

# Shell hook
shell_hook = true

# MCP server port (when using full MCP mode)
mcp_port = 0  # 0 = auto-select</code></pre>

  <h2>Session</h2>
  <pre><code>[session]
# Persist sessions across restarts
persist = true

# Auto-compress after N tool calls
auto_compress_after = 15

# Knowledge storage
knowledge_path = "~/.local/share/lean-ctx/knowledge"</code></pre>

  <h2>Budget</h2>
  <pre><code>[budget]
# Max tokens per session (0 = unlimited)
token_limit = 0

# Max cost per session in USD (0 = unlimited)
cost_limit = 0.0

# Max shell commands per session (0 = unlimited)
shell_limit = 0</code></pre>

  <h2>Output</h2>
  <pre><code>[output]
# Output hints (append helpful context to responses)
compressed_hint = true
related_hint = false
verify_footer = true
archive_hint = false</code></pre>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <pre><code>[security]
# PathJail: restrict to project directory
path_jail = true

# Max file size to read (bytes)
max_file_size = 10485760  # 10MB

# Block known secret patterns
secret_detection = true</code></pre>

  <h2>Profiles</h2>
  <p>Profiles bundle multiple settings for specific use cases. See <a href="/docs/governance/">Governance</a> for built-in profiles.</p>
  <pre><code>[profile]
# Active profile: default | minimal | verbose | paranoid
active = "default"</code></pre>
</DocsLayout>
